# ===== RUN 4: held-out test of code6_sb4 =====
# Pre-registration, written after the fit and before any run-4 load (sha256 99bf2ee8e5af691f93f42561fbef9eb4a38ca708a628a084789e0cc74210041d):
#   written_utc 2026-10-12T19:23:55Z, before any run-4 arm has been loaded. Held-out test of a model FITTED on run 3.
#   run 3 (prereg ca48cd0d...): controls 15:0, 1:0, 16:8, 16:15, 10:12 all EXACT, so the 0x7B site moves the bias shift.
#     Its pre-registered predictions for shift_bias > 15 and for bytes >= 63 / negative bytes MISSED. The post-hoc fit
#     (scratch fit_patch3.txt, mism_patch3.txt; tool --rescore) is model code6_sb4:
#       vsrs code = shift_cut byte & 63 (the byte itself, NOT sigma = shift_cut + 14); 0..59 shift right with half_up rounding,
#       60..63 shift left by 4..1; a left shift saturates only if a ONE-bit shift would overflow int8 (t outside [-64, 63]),
#       otherwise t << k wraps to 8 bits; effective shift_bias = shift_bias & 15.
#     It reproduces all 36 run-3 arms exactly (rescore3.txt) and run 2's (bytes 46..50 are right shifts there).
#     Rival sigma6_sb4 (sigma wrapped to 6 bits) fails run-3 arms 50:24, -8, -14.
